<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51185" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσότιμ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>equal in honour</i> or
				<i>privilege</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ʼΑπόλλων</span>
			(i.e. sharing the honours paid to Zeus) <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				234.25
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i>CR Acad.Inscr.</i><i><span class="en">
				1906.419
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Alabanda</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ θεὸς . . -ον παρέχι τράπεζαν τοῖς
					ὁποθενοῦν ἀφικνουμένοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BCH</u>
					51.73
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Panamara</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πίστις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>2 Ep.Pet.</u>
					1.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ πρῶτοι καὶ ἰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				19
			</span></i>, cf. Wilcken <i><span class="en">
				<u>Chr.</u>
				13.10
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
			</span></i><i>D Mort.</i><i><span class="en">
				24.3
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεις τισί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.Chr.
					41.2
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότεροι, τοῖς κρατοῦσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					39.4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἰ.</span>,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσοτιμία</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.246
			</span></i>; of a person, <i>maintaining equality of privilege</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				2.4.9
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μως, τινάς τισιν ἄγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					5.177c
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῶντα δικαίως καὶ ἰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				544.34
			</span></i> (Ancyra, <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				4032.5
			</span></i> (ibid.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IGRom.</u>
				3.195
			</span></i> (ibid.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. ἔχουσι πρὸς ἀλλήλους οἱ ὅροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phlp.
					<u>in APr.</u>
					167.14
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aphr.
				<u>in Metaph.</u>
				241.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>equal in value</i>: hence, <i>equal</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμάρτημα ἀκούσιον ἰ. ἑκουσίῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.248
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἰ. δυσέφικτον ἐν ταῖς ἀμοιβαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
					2.3.6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. μάχη</span>
			<i>evenly balanced</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				10.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> as title of
			rank at the Ptolemaic court, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἰσοτίμων τοῖς πρώτοις φίλοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PRyl.</u>
					66
				</span></i>
			 intr., <i><span class="en">
				253
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Arch.Pap.</u>
				6.372
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
